The following <%= "community".pluralize(@communities.size) %> <%= @communities.size == 1 ? "has" : "have" %> been deactivated due to inactivity and <%= @communities.size == 1 ? "is" : "are" %> ready for deletion:

<% @communities.each do |community| %>
- <%= community.name %> (slug: <%= community.slug %>, id: <%= community.id %>, deactivated: <%= l(community.deactivated_at.to_date) %>)
<% end %>

Deactivated communities cannot be signed into or used. To permanently delete them, paste the
following into the production Rails console. Replace YOUR_SUPER_ADMIN_USER_ID with your
numeric user ID (must be a super_admin, e.g. User.find_by(email: "you@gather.coop").id).

---
actor_id = YOUR_SUPER_ADMIN_USER_ID

[
<% @communities.each do |community| %>  [<%= community.id %>, "<%= community.name %>"],
<% end %>].each do |community_id, name|
  CommunityDeletionJob.perform_later(community_id, actor_id)
  puts "Queued deletion for #{name} (id=#{community_id})"
end
---

This notice will repeat weekly until each community is deleted.
